{"title":"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Full_Coordinate_Bash_for_x_and_y)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Full Coordinate Bash for x and y)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Alternate_solution_in_finding_x)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Alternate solution in finding x)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_Clear_Explanation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution Clear Explanation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Other_video_solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Other video solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is inscribed in a right triangle with sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so that one vertex of the square coincides with the right-angle vertex of the triangle. A square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is inscribed in another right triangle with sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so that one side of the square lies on the hypotenuse of the triangle. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46d783347dc9059f615d5444a5ec6e23df3229ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529a2fdd289a0bf2ce24116e5f33d1419b26eb0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\dfrac{12}{13} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\dfrac{35}{37} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac{37}{35} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\dfrac{13}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"404\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Analyze the first right triangle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d8d4056c8f797b4635c3aa467fd8f36bb9281c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C; pair D, e, F; A = (0,0); B = (4,0); C = (0,3);  D = (0, 12/7); e = (12/7 , 12/7); F = (12/7, 0);  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(D--e--F);  label(&quot;$x$&quot;, D/2, W); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, e, NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa8d493eebaf7cccb91cb38faf5e8603c2b36cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle FBE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are similar, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aabbdd33c8976adf688d8c5efc9b4f7476dba6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BF}{FE} = \\frac{AB}{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. This can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7baea4362d71aff2b243e467018804f46cc2d71f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4-x}{x}=\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"37\" />. Solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58a64f6c40f0b01342db16e6e944c641ac2fa13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{12}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Now we analyze the second triangle.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/c/abc0a7730ccae9580fa62d17f8130c558ceec4bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C; pair q, R, S, T; A = (0,0); B = (4,0); C = (0,3);  q = (1.297, 0); R = (2.27 , 1.297); S = (0.973, 2.27); T  = (0, 0.973);  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(q--R--S--T--cycle);  label(&quot;$y$&quot;, (q+R)/2, NW); label(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;$C&#39;$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, (q-(0,0.3))); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, NE); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, S, NE); label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T, W); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a764854d1073fac0a788e874db580d732c7c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f287563f368176de746a39a18b5bd9f67a4ae2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle RB&#39;Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9202224090ff91f70ae08a568084e09de400b94e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle C&#39;ST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"19\" /> are similar, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eaeb75a8123b0e761ebde2ad2690ef5e7c1e7981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RB&#39; = \\frac{4}{3}y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319cd04f03e14b5157aac45c2f88dda996f66dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;S = \\frac{3}{4}y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c8841c95a5d0a7a1e2d8b9ab309aefb1eabda1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C&#39;B&#39; = C&#39;S + SR + RB&#39; = \\frac{4}{3}y + y + \\frac{3}{4}y = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"354\" height=\"38\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9448b5df6dc8deff1d35c0dddd4c87416474a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{60}{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9f96fea9b26efe71f4125c194e4342084953618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\:\\frac{37}{35}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Full_Coordinate_Bash_for_x_and_y.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Full_Coordinate_Bash_for_x_and_y)\">Solution 2 (Full Coordinate Bash for x and y)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Full Coordinate Bash for x and y)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set the right-angle vertex of the triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that the hypotenuse of the triangle can be described by the line equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e0407f07dc93344bb0ba27bf0d08d97bd0ffe87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3 - \\frac{3}{4}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/4/8644070a7f4f06c1259c96de95a07a2ffe44db73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y - 12 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the top-right vertex of the first square lies on this hypotenuse and can be described by the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, we may solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780954cf945eb7815eed9beea24c8ee22992fb8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58a64f6c40f0b01342db16e6e944c641ac2fa13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{12}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, let the two corners of the second square that touch the sides of the triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafebda588d01006c49fe7f72623f1a9a79cfd8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x_Q, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab3aef3503bec67b466876dc5424153f2ca9498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(0, y_T)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />. Pushing these points straight out by a distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> gives the other two corners on the hypotenuse:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb9686e21012b932162a2b00ad984a025d296fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = \\left(x_Q + \\frac{3}{5}y, \\frac{4}{5}y\\right)\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/9030f1a3bc9538035d70cca214078085e572b8c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\left(\\frac{3}{5}y, y_T + \\frac{4}{5}y\\right)\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the hypotenuse line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7cd6eb9cb4c8961668dd28f1514be7da746ec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />, we can plug them in to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064df96f0186da2e2ab8337173c8b3b81a62fe90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8cc8c8d702997a3af13dfe07a1aa7a65e3f3be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87ac193dbb7d8b02d5aa49578bc6df92f1aa1782.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\left(x_Q + \\frac{3}{5}y\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac{4}{5}y\\right) = 12 \\implies x_Q = \\frac{12-5y}{3}\\]\" width=\"387\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d621d470df424958d568e788a20ae5030b7de51e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\left(\\frac{3}{5}y\\right) + 4\\left(y_T + \\frac{4}{5}y\\right) = 12 \\implies y_T = \\frac{12-5y}{4}\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The distance between the two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is just the side of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Using the distance formula:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf80764c68882687c041614a796dbcae7a5b9f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{12-5y}{3}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{12-5y}{4}\\right)^2 = y^2\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92adddc474550f0e39cecfd4d5ce8d35fe5adc06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(12-5y)^2 \\left(\\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{1}{16}\\right) = y^2\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25ea98d94a12e70a7af9dc7cf64d50cb6aee5098.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(12-5y)^2 \\left(\\frac{25}{144}\\right) = y^2\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Taking the square root of both sides gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/213e6aa802e287b8ead527368440a54401f3d99c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5}{12}(12-5y) = y \\implies 60 - 25y = 12y \\implies 37y = 60 \\implies y = \\frac{60}{37}\\]\" width=\"520\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/c/0cc9e64c5f69d85d7de9af17f5e7156f94bcaf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} = \\frac{12/7}{60/37} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\:\\frac{37}{35}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"181\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Alternate_solution_in_finding_x.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Alternate_solution_in_finding_x)\">Solution 3 (Alternate solution in finding x)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Alternate solution in finding x)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set the right-angle vertex of the triangle as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that the hypotenuse of the triangle, as depicted in solution one, can be described by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e0407f07dc93344bb0ba27bf0d08d97bd0ffe87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3 - \\frac{3}{4}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> can be describe by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, we may solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by solving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/03163221c642d8c907a41f91bdaea5563fd3a4cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3- \\frac{3}{4}x = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cacf43686d65900ea166cd9e79a446f5dd448394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Proceed by finding the value of y via the method described in solution 1, and we will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c9448b5df6dc8deff1d35c0dddd4c87416474a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{60}{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9f96fea9b26efe71f4125c194e4342084953618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\:\\frac{37}{35}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In general, if the legs were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, we have that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b30c8ba4cf4162a8e3849e16f7c2bceaaad553.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x= \\frac{ab}{a+b}, y=\\frac{ab\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}{a^2+ab+b^2}.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"42\" /> \nThis can be verified by plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda5328bc4703ff88e62aa83ea58ae4e8361f5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.\n~anduran\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_Clear_Explanation\">Video Solution Clear Explanation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution Clear Explanation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IJWyE6kI7mo?si=0jYMJuWfSIHPrpow\">https://youtu.be/IJWyE6kI7mo?si=0jYMJuWfSIHPrpow</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DJ1105lcJJM?si=Z24jb7mCjzjLPdKh\">https://youtu.be/DJ1105lcJJM?si=Z24jb7mCjzjLPdKh</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other_video_solutions\">Other video solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Other video solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/THeq4ZiZxIA\">https://youtu.be/THeq4ZiZxIA</a>\n-Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MF2QFOInbYc\">https://youtu.be/MF2QFOInbYc</a>\n-Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A\">2017 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n